{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKVwNCSZBiybE2Vpn4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**No, not on these terms. Make a counter-offer instead of turning them down outright.**\n\n**Why not as offered**\n\n- **The timeline doesn't add up.** Sales says the work is two engineers for two quarters, about six months. The deadline is four months. Sales estimates are usually low, so to hit four months you'd likely need three or four of your five engineers. That stalls the independents strategy for most of the year.\n- **No commitment yet.** Without a signed contract, or even a letter of intent, you'd be building custom features on a promise. If they walk away in month four, you've spent around 40% or more of your engineering capacity on nothing.\n- **It's a different market.** A 40-site hotel group is a different buyer from your target. Expect more procurement and security reviews, ongoing custom requests, and hotel-specific payroll needs. Their demands would steer your roadmap away from independents.\n- **Concentration risk.** One customer worth four times your largest would hold a lot of power over pricing and priorities.\n\n**What's worth keeping**\n\n- Multi-entity reporting probably helps your own 3–5-site customers. Approval chains might too. Single sign-on (SSO) mostly doesn't.\n- The revenue is real and could extend your runway.\n\n**Suggested counter-offer**\n\n1. Ask for a signed contract, or at least a letter of intent with a deposit or termination fee, before any build starts.\n2. Ask for a six-month timeline delivered in milestones, with payment tied to each one.\n3. Commit first to the parts that also serve independents, such as multi-entity reporting. Leave SSO and fully custom approval chains to a later phase or a paid add-on.\n4. Get your engineers to estimate the work properly before you agree to any dates.\n\nIf they won't sign anything or move the deadline, walk away. If they will, it becomes a well-funded way to build features you'd want anyway."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3195,"cache_read_input_tokens":5033,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3195},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"46639c1d-c852-4128-8d37-03c54bb3ec4d","uuid":"571ac87a-d058-4700-8781-64856b6e3a1a","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:28:29.911Z","request_id":"req_011CftKVw93hWgfkjW9q5J3r"}
